===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Concerning or relating to [[politics]], the [[art]] and [[process]] of [[govern|governing]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Political''' principles are rarely absolute, as '''political''' logic holds an imperfect result by compromise is better than a theoretically perfect abstention from the political process in the opposition.}}
#* {{RQ:Birmingham Gossamer|chapter=I|passage=As a '''political''' system democracy seems to me extraordinarily foolish, but I would not go out of my way to protest against it. My servant is, so far as I am concerned, welcome to as many votes as he can get. I would very gladly make mine over to him if I could.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=2012-01|author=Philip E. Mirowski|volume=100|issue=1|page=87|magazine=w:American Scientist|title=Harms to Health from the Pursuit of Profits|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/harms-to-health-from-the-pursuit-of-profits|passage=In an era when '''political''' leaders promise deliverance from decline through America’s purported preeminence in scientific research, the news that science is in deep trouble in the United States has been as unwelcome as a diagnosis of leukemia following the loss of health insurance.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20140909005026/https://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/harms-to-health-from-the-pursuit-of-profits|archivedate=9 September 2014}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=2012-11-07|author=Matt Bai|title=Winning a Second Term, Obama Will Confront Familiar Headwinds|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/in-president-obamas-second-term-familiar-challenges.html?pagewanted=all&_r=0
|passage=That brief moment after the election four years ago, when many Americans thought Mr. Obama’s election would presage a new, less fractious '''political''' era, now seems very much a thing of the past.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160610194024/https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/in-president-obamas-second-term-familiar-challenges.html?pagewanted=all&_r=0|archivedate=2016-06-10}}
# Concerning a [[polity]] or its administrative components.
#: {{ux|en|Good '''political''' staff is hard to find, they may neither be ambitious and corrupted by power nor tempted by private sector careers.}}
# {{lb|en|pejorative}} [[inappropriately|Inappropriately]] [[motivate|motivated]] by political calculation, as it pertains to [[elections]], [[power dynamics]], [[ideologies]], etc.
#: {{ux|en|The media alleged that the Federal Reserve chairman’s decision to cut rates before the election was '''political'''.}}
# Of or relating to views about social relationships that involve power, standing, influence or conflict.
# {{lb|en|of a person}} Interested in [[politics]].

